From 6cab7c4578d0d4c460434b0f13b7da4130fb93e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=E5=AD=90=E8=AA=89?=
 <9528147+zi-yu1983@user.noreply.gitee.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 09:00:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 038/168] fix(installer): embed frontendDist on every dist
 rebuild
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tauri 2 codegen runs at compile time and embeds apps/bootstrap-installer/dist/
into the binary via include_bytes!. Without a `cargo:rerun-if-changed=../dist`
directive, cargo's build script has no signal that the dist/ directory changed,
so a `npm run build` that updates vite asset hashes (e.g. KaTeX_Main-Regular-ypZvNtVU.ttf)
does not retrigger a rebuild. The resulting binary contains stale embedded files,
the webview's index.html references asset hashes that no longer exist, and the
user sees a blue screen at launch.

The fix forces the build script to re-run on any dist mutation, so tauri-build
re-embeds the current dist and the embed pipeline is self-healing.

Staging range: apps/bootstrap-installer/src-tauri/{build.rs, src/install_script.rs, src/lib.rs}
- build.rs: + cargo:rerun-if-changed=../dist (14 lines incl. comment)
- install_script.rs: INSTALL_SCRIPT_REPOSITORY = "ZIYU-FUI/wenshu" (fork URL)
- lib.rs: eprintln + tracing setup callback diagnostics

Verified: 5/5 PM-direct AC (build success, frontend embed grep KaTeX 1 hit,
DBVGDLLs 1 hit, binary 7.3MB, setup callback entered, headless WebKit React UI
rendered "Starting 文枢..." instead of blue screen).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
